>> title: Suadero
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, brisket, mexican, confit, tacos, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: suadero, res, taco de suadero, tacos de suadero, rose meat, brisket flap
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-roja
>> servings: 8
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: narrow — the fat has to shiver rather than spit: anything hotter fries the beef, and a fried brisket never pulls apart

>> step: salt the beef
Season @beef brisket{2%lb}(900 g; the flat, in one piece) and @beef navel{1%lb}(450 g; or another pound of brisket) all over with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}.

>> step: render the fat 10 min
Render @lard{1%lb}(450 g) with @white onion{1/2}(halved), @garlic{4%cloves}, and @bay leaves{2} in a wide #cazuela{} over low heat for ~render{10%min}, until the aromatics sizzle without colouring.

>> step: simmer barely covered 2 hr
Simmer @&(~2)salted beef{} in @&(~1)warm fat{}, barely covered and never bubbling hard, for ~simmer{2%hr}, until it pulls apart under a spoon. The fat should shiver rather than spit.

>> step: chop on the board
Chop @&(~1)confited beef{} on the board into rough small pieces, fat and all.

>> step: crisp on the comal 4 min
Crisp @&(~1)chopped suadero{} on a hot #comal{} in @rendered fat{2%Tbs}(spooned off the pot) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} for ~sear{4%min}, until the edges catch.
